  "title": "Prostate biopsy",
  "description": "A prostate biopsy collects tissue samples from your prostate to diagnose cancer or confirm high PSA levels. During this quick outpatient procedure, your urologist uses ultrasound guidance to direct a needle into the prostate and remove small tissue samples. The procedure takes 10-15 minutes and you're given local anesthesia for comfort. Afterward, you may have slight blood in your urine or semen for a few days, completely normal. Most people experience minimal discomfort. Results guide decisions about treatment or monitoring. You go home the same day and resume normal activities within a few days.",
